        "titulo": "The compound future: «буду» + infinitive",
        "explicacao": "In English the future is made with \"will\" (\"I will read\") or \"going to\" (\"I'm going to read\"). Russian has TWO forms of the future, depending on the aspect. The first is the compound future, of the imperfective: «буду» + imperfective infinitive = I will do / I will be doing (process, habit, duration). The verb «быть» in the future: я буду, ты будешь, он будет, мы будем, вы будете, они будут. The verb that follows always stays in the infinitive.",
        "comparacao": "English says \"I will read\", which looks a lot like this: «буду» works like \"will be\", followed by the infinitive. «Буду читать» is like \"I will be reading\" (for a while, regularly).",
